From 4c2acf6a385102abb3e2bf60982d0bffdb61932a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eden PS4 <eden-ps4@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 07:23:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS4 fastmem: an arena clear of the GPU windows, accesses past
 it walked inline, a cheaper range check, groups with the shared walk

03.85's arena (2^38 at 512 GiB: 2^39 didn't fit above it) went unused with Unsafe accuracy (the
launcher now sets cpuopt_unsafe_host_mmu). Its arena is tried at 288 GiB first (the GPU windows
take 256-288 GiB), for 2^39.

dynarmic, A64 fastmem:
- an access past the arena (a 2^38 arena, a 39-bit game) does the page table walk inline
  (EmitA64FastmemRangeWalk, deferred), the fallback only if that fails, instead of calling the
  callbacks every time;
- the range check is one compare with the limit in the constant pool, not a copy, a shift and a
  scratch register;
- A64SharedWalkPass runs with fastmem too: a group of loads and stores through one base walks
  once, a lone access uses fastmem (the walk and the arena reach the same memory).

Host harness (memfd-backed guest memory mapped into a 2^32 arena, the marked and unmapped pages
left out): four dependent loads 15.3-18.6 -> 7.4-7.9 ns, a call with a prologue and struct
accesses 11.9 -> 11.1 ns; 700 random load/store and 500 exclusive programs agree with the page
table, with every access in the arena or every access past it.
